[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Reviewing the CHANGE note that claims coverage of cycle errors, priority-ordered topological sort and critical path, and the FAIL_FAST/SKIP_DOWNSTREAM/CONTINUE_ON_ERROR wave transitions, the suite leaves five specification aspects unasserted: the postcondition that WHEN a cycle exists the graph contracts MUST raise CycleError containing the cycle sequence is verified only for a closed two-node cycle and never for cyclic nodes that also carry acyclic prerequisites; the critical-path postconditions that MUST return the sequence of nodes forming the longest path and MUST return the cumulative weight of that path are never verified for graphs whose several upstream branches tie on earliest completion time, so no assertion confirms the returned sequence is a longest path of the correct total weight under ties; the same critical-path postconditions are never verified for a graph containing no nodes, whose longest path is the empty sequence with weight zero; the mark_succeeded postcondition that a dependent currently PENDING is promoted to READY only when all its upstream dependencies are SUCCEEDED is never verified for the interaction in which that dependent has already been transitioned to SKIPPED by SKIP_DOWNSTREAM before a remaining prerequisite subsequently SUCCEEDS; and the SKIP_DOWNSTREAM postcondition that MUST transition all transitive dependents to SKIPPED is never verified for a downstream dependent reachable through more than one of its upstream dependency chains.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: The CHANGE note describes validation with cycle detection, priority-ordered topological sort, and sequential wave execution, yet four guarded statements are unreachable under the specification closure: the validation depth-first guard that skips a dependency absent from the graph is unreachable because the preceding completeness pass already raises NodeNotFoundError for any missing dependency, and the assumption pragma currently sits on a standalone comment line so the guarded branch itself is still counted as uncovered; the topological-sort guard that skips a downstream dependent absent from the in-degree mapping is unreachable because every dependent is by construction a registered node; the cycle-locator recursion fallback that returns False after exhausting an upstream branch is unreachable because every node with residual non-zero in-degree always retains an unresolved upstream dependency chain that must revisit an active node and therefore always reports a cycle; and the run wave-loop guard that skips a node whose state is no longer READY is unreachable because FAIL_FAST halts the wave immediately after the failing node while successful transitions only promote PENDING dependents outside the current wave, so no contract-valid transition can make a later wave member non-READY before its turn. Restructure these sites to eliminate the unreachable code, or annotate the guarded statements themselves with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)' stating the guaranteeing contract assumption.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Addresses all five feedback gaps: (1) validate CycleError now asserted for a cycle reachable through an acyclic prerequisite, checking the reported cycle contains only cyclic nodes; (2) critical path asserted for an empty graph (empty path, zero weight); (3) critical path asserted under tied upstream branch completion times, verifying the returned sequence is one of the longest paths and the weight equals its cumulative weight; (4) mark_succeeded asserted not to revive a dependent already SKIPPED by SKIP_DOWNSTREAM when a remaining prerequisite later succeeds; (5) SKIP_DOWNSTREAM asserted to mark a diamond dependent reachable through multiple upstream chains as SKIPPED.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Eliminate unreachable defensive branches flagged by feedback: remove the validate DFS missing-dependency guard (the completeness pass already raises NodeNotFoundError for every missing dependency), remove the topological-sort dependent-membership guard (every dependent is a registered node by construction and present in the in-degree map), replace the recursive cycle locator with a deterministic residual-graph walk that always closes a cycle and has no unreachable fallback return, and remove the run wave-loop READY-state guard (FAIL_FAST halts the wave immediately and success only promotes PENDING dependents outside the current wave, so every later wave member remains READY). Behavioral contracts and runtime results are unchanged.
